  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1221 PM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nThursday-Monday, another shortwave to drop south in the northwest \nflow aloft on Thursday. Guidance continues to show largely dry \nconditions through the day Thursday, but areas east of the \nMississippi River will have the potential for brief light \nprecipitation. Looking at the environment, we are generally looking \nat isolated to widely scattered showers passing through the cyclonic \nflow overhead. Although, this is low confidence and PoPs remain \n<15%. Our higher confidence is with the cooler air that will advect \nin through Thursday, keeping temperatures near to slightly below \nnormal through Saturday. High temperatures are expected to drop into \nthe low-mid 40s, with nights in the 20s to around 30. A large area \nof high pressure builds over the region through the weekend, slowly \ntracking east into next week. While overhead, temperatures will \nremain near seasonal normals with light winds and dry conditions. As \nthis tracks east into next week, temperatures will return to above \nseasonal normals, roughly in the 50s early next week. Dry conditions \nare currently expected to remain through the start of next week, \nowing to lacking moisture return.",
